=== layout: title-content

# Strands

@body

- Template
- Complimentary
- Anti-sense
- Read 3&prime; to 5&prime;
- Non-template
- Actual Sequence
- Sense
- Read 5&prime; to 3&prime;

=== layout: title-only

# Complementary Sequences

=== layout: title-content

# 1. Which one of the following sequences is complimentary to the sequence `ATGC`?

@body

  - A. `CGTA`
  - B. `CGAT`
  - C. `GCTA`
  - D. `TACG`
  - E. `ATGC`
- Answer: D

=== layout: title-content

# 2. Which one of the following DNA sequences is complimentary to the direction-less DNA sequence `CGC,ATA,GG`?

@body

  - A. `GGA,TAC,GC`
  - B. `GCG,TTA,GG`
  - C. `CGC,AAT,CC`
  - D. `GCG,TAT,CC`
  - E. `GCG,TCC,TA`
- Answer: D

=== layout: title-content

# 3. Which one of the following sequences is complimentary to the sequence 5&prime;-`ATGC`-3&prime;?

@body

  - A. 5&prime;-`CGTA`-3&prime;
  - B. 5&prime;-`GCAT`-3&prime;
  - C. 5&prime;-`CGAT`-3&prime;
  - D. 5&prime;-`TACG`-3&prime;
  - E. 5&prime;-`ATGC`-3&prime;
- Answer: B
- 3&prime;-`TACG`-5&prime;

=== layout: title-content

# 4. Which one of the following sequences is complimentary to the sequence

@body

- 3&prime;-`CAA,AGG,T`-5&prime;?
  - Hint: pay attention to the 5&prime; and 3&prime; directions!
  - A. 5&prime;-`GTT,TCC,A`-3&prime;
  - B. 5&prime;-`CAA,AGG,T`-3&prime;
  - C. 5&prime;-`ACC,TTT,G`-3&prime;
  - D. 5&prime;-`TGG,AAA,C`-3&prime;
  - E. 5&prime;-`TGG,TCC,A`-3&prime;
- Answer: A

